From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3dx9: tangent frames, D3DXConcatenateMeshes, D3DXLoadMeshFromXof (3512)

d3dx9: tangent frames, D3DXComputeTangent, D3DXConcatenateMeshes, D3DXLoadMeshFromXof

D3DXComputeTangentFrameEx computes the u and v partial derivatives of the position (tangent and
binormal) from the texture coordinates per face, weights them like the normals (angle, area, equal),
averages over the point representatives, orthogonalises them against the normal unless told not to, and
honours WRAP_U/V, WIND_CW, DONT_NORMALIZE_PARTIALS and ORTHOGONALIZE_FROM_U/V. Without
GENERATE_IN_PLACE it returns a copy of the mesh that has the missing output elements added, and the
identity vertex mapping. D3DXComputeTangentFrame and D3DXComputeTangent are built on it.
D3DXConcatenateMeshes joins meshes into one (vertex data converted to the output declaration, geometry
and texture matrices applied, indices offset, attributes kept). D3DXLoadMeshFromXof loads a mesh from an
ID3DXFileData as D3DXLoadSkinMeshFromXof does, without the skin.
